Subject: Windows joke >:) (fwd)
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.3.91.960117225659.212A-100000@HayStack.dooms-land.hell>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Status: RO
X-Status: 



>A Windows programmer dies of a heart attack.  He finds his soul floating away
>from his body, and suddenly guided by an Angel.
>
>The Angel brings him to a
>place on the beach, with rock'n'roll playing, and beautiful people playing
>volleyball and drinking free soda.  "WOW!" says the Windows programmer.  "Is
>this Heaven?"  "No," the Angel says, "This is Hell."
>
>Then the Angel brings
>him to another place with no noise at all, just a vast world of old people
>sitting on park benches throwing popcorn at dead birds.  "This is heaven."
>The Angel says.  "You may choose where to go."
>
>The Windows programmer says,
>"Hell!" and is immediately teleported to a pool of molten lava.  "Ahhh!!!
>This isn't what you showed me!!" He screams.
>
>The Angel replies "That was the demo."

regards,

