(translated from hebrew)

A Jewish Polish woman was standing on the balcony with her neibour
(Jewish Polish woman of the same brand). They notice that her husband is 
approaching the house with a bouquette of flowers in his hand.

"oh my god!" exclaims the Polish woman.
"now i'm going to have to stay awake all night with my ass up in the air 
and my legs wide open.."
"but why ?" asks the neibour, "don't you have a vase for that ?"


