Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.3.91-heb-2.05.960414223019.18157B-100000@xpert.com>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Sender: owner-fun@fun
Precedence: bulk
Status: RO
X-Status: 


A story forwarded from a voice story a friend told me:


One day he was driving in his Subaru. His car was all messed up and had 
mud on it, because he was driving in the fields of his father. Well, the 
kind of car you wouldn't want to buy. Stopping by the traffic lights, he 
saw a neat Pontiac Grand Prix near him. He slowly opened the window, and 
shouted - " Hey, you take my car, I take yours? " well... the man said 
" Yeah, you take my LEGS, I take yours? "




should be forwarded to "not_so_funny@xpert.com".




 - Shahar.

