From: Omer Zak <xlacha1@wicc.weizmann.ac.il>
To: fun@xpert.com
Subject: humor (a Christian religious joke)
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.3.91.960520230112.114D-100000@wicc.weizmann.ac.il>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Sender: owner-fun@fun
Precedence: bulk
Status: RO
X-Status: 


    A man is driving down a deserted stretch of highway, when he no-
 ticed a sign out of the corner of his eye.  It read: SISTERS OF MERCY
 HOUSE OF PROSTITUTION 10 MILES.  He thought it was a figment of his
 imagination and drove on without a second thought.  Soon, he saw
 another sign which read: SISTERS OF MERCY HOUSE OF PROSTITUTION 5
 MILES and realized that these signs are for real.
    As he drove past a third sign saying: SISTERS OF MERCY HOUSE OF
 PROSTITUTION NEXT RIGHT, his curiosity got the best of him and he
 pulled into the drive.
    On the far side of the parking lot is a somber stone building with
 a small sign next to the door which read SISTERS OF MERCY.  He climbed
 the steps and rang the bell.  The door is answered by a nun in a long
 black habit who asked, "What may we do for you, my son?"
    He answered, "I saw your signs along the highway, and was inter-
 ested in possibly doing business."
    "Very well, my son.  Please follow me."  He is led through many
 winding passages and is soon quite disoriented. The nun stopped at a
 closed door, and told the man, "Please knock on this door."
    He did as he was told and this door is answered by another nun in
 a long habit and holding a tin cup.  The nun instructed, "Please place
 $50 in the cup, then go through the large wooden door at the end of
 this hallway."
    He got $50 out of his wallet and placed it in the second nun's cup. 
 He trotted eagerly down the hall and slipped through the door, pulling
 it shut behind him.  As the door locked behind him, he found himself
 back in the parking lot, facing another small sign:

   GO IN PEACE, YOU HAVE JUST BEEN SCREWED BY THE SISTERS OF MERCY.

