A priest and a rabbi were golfing one day and the conversation turned to
their religious taboos.

The priest asked the rabbi, "I know you keep kosher, but have you ever
even TASTED pork?"

The rabbi admitted, that yes, many years ago he had eaten pork against his
religous laws.

Then rabbi asked, "I know you have taken a vow of celibacy, but have you
ever...."

The priest admitted he had, in fact, broken his vow of celibacy.

The rabbi turned a wry smile.  "Better than pork, ain't it?"

