It was about a month ago when a Dutchman in Amsterdam felt that he needed
to confess, so went to the local priest.
    "Forgive me Father, for I have sinned. During WWII I hid a Jew in my
attic."
    "Well," answered the priest, "that's not a sin."
    "But I charged him for 20 Gulden for every week he stayed there."
"I admit that wasn't good, but you did it for a good cause."
    "Yes, but I haven't told him that the war is over."



