To: fun@xpert.com
Subject: (Fwd) Joke
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Sender: owner-fun@fun
Precedence: bulk
Status: RO
X-Status: 



A priest, a minister and a rabbi are playing golf. A foursome before them
delays them by excrutiatingly slow play. After 3 hours, the priest goes to
complain to the golf pro, who tells him: "They play slowly because they're
blind." "I'm humbled, says the priest, what admirable perseverance in the
face of adversity! I'm going to write a sermon on this for Sunday". Next,
the minister goes to complain. "They're blind", says the pro. "This is a
lesson in the fortitude of the human spirit! I'm ashamed I complained. I'm
going to organize a tournament for blind players." Finally the rabbi asks
"Why are these people so slow?" "They're blind."  "So why can't they play at
night?".

