Q: How many software documenters does it take to change a light bulb?
A: None. They document it as a bug.

Q: How many programmers...?
A: None. They document it as a feature.

Q: How many Microsoft staff...?
A: None. They set it as the standard condition.

Q: How many Bill Gates?
A: None. He just moves to another room in his palace.

Q: How many Israelis?
A: Four. One to change it, and three to put a sign: "Here will be done
   a project of changing a light bulb, at a cost of 11 Shekels."

And the original joke:

Q: How many polish does it take to change a light bulb?
A: Four. One to hold it, and three to turn him around.
