Precedence: bulk
Status: RO
X-Status: 


This, guys, is a REAL story.

I won't mention the name of the bank, since I know some laws about this...

One day, I opened myself an account on one of this "Direct" banks. after a
few days I got a phone call from the bank, and a nice lady told me I can
have one year of an international credit card for free.
So, after a few days of thinking, I called back - and said - "okay, I want
this free ##### Card" (sorry, no names....). so the nice guy said - 
"Oh, you don't order it here".  I said - "They called me and said I should
order it here!" and he said "No. you cant order it here." I was confused,
so I ask - Do I have to GO to the bank? and he answered - "NO, you can ask
me to order it for you."
totaly confused I gave him the details. He said the card will be in 4
days.
After 4 days my bank called me. "DID YOU ORDER A ##### CARD?" asked a nice
man. "Yes, I did" I said, hoping to hear nice news. "WHY???? YOU DONT NEED
IT. YOU ARE A STUDENT". after a long argue - I got my card.

So.... the days passed and I called the bank to know how much did I pay
for my monthly credit charges. The nice lady said it's XXXX shekels. so
the day after, while using the KASPOMAT for having some money, I saw i
have 500 shekels less than expected. The phone call to the bank made it
all clear - the Credit charge was 500 more than they said. I asked the guy
how can it happen - and his answer was :
"NEVER TRUST OR BELIEVE THOSE DIRECT BANK. ALWAYS CHECK WHAT THEY SAY
TWICE".
so now I do.

Two days ago I found out I have 1000 Shekels less than I should. So I
checked it out and I found a mistake of the bank - They charged me 1120nis
for a 120nis check. they gave me 1120 back and took 120 again, to correct
this. I called the bank to check if they did it as promised..... and found
out there were 2 deposits of 1120nis to my account..... 
actually - there is a bug in the system - which shows every transaction
twice while the system updates it, which is only a few minutes every
day.... and i called at this exact time.... so my account had some more
money in it.... So let us think what would have happened if the deposit
was 1G shekels? :-)

And the last story was when I called the bank to buy some Pound Sterlings,
for my holiday in England.

I asked - what is the rate for it? and the lady said - for sale - it's
5.00 shekels for one pound. I said - "Okay, I want 300". 
now - I should mention that they charge you nothing for the exchange.
So the lady said - "OKAY, I'll make it 25 bills of 10 Pounds". I said - a
little confused - "no, make some of it 50 pounds, and make it 300, not
250". so she said - "okay, that will be 3 x 50 bills, and 10 x 10 pounds
bills". I tried to correct her, gently saying "no, make it 4 x 50". so she
said - "okay, 4 x 50 and 5 x 10". 
I was tired. so I said - "MAKE IT 10X10 and 4X50". 
she said "That'l be 300 pounds".
I said - "Right."
she said - "which is 300 x 5, which makes = 1578".
after a long argue she found out there is a rate of 5.29 which is a
"spare" they take so you will have enough money to buy it, and won't have
surprises if the rate goes up.....


Love you all, 

 Shahar Raz.
 


