When Albert Einstein was saying a few words about Technology in a
University, one of the students asked - "Mr. Einstein, How exactly does a
RADIO work?"

A.E. said - "Young sir, first you have to understand the Telegraph:
             A telegraph is like a long cat - It's tail is in L.A, and 
	     it's head is in N.Y, so when you pull his tail in L.A., his
             mouth cries in N.Y."

Everyone in the room smiled, and loved the idea.

	    "Now," said A.E., "a RADIO is like a telegraph, without the
             cat"





Shahar.

